   "group": "United States",
   "headline": "Nasdaq 100 slips into a correction as doubts about AI spending grow",
   "when": "Mon 2 Nov · US close",
   "what": "US shares ended lower on Monday. The S&P 500 fell 0.51% to 7,541.40 and the Nasdaq fell 1.07% to 25,164. Bloomberg reports the Nasdaq 100 entered a correction as big-tech results fed worries about AI spending. CoinDesk notes the Nasdaq went from a 1% gain to a 1% loss during the day. Oil fell sharply on hopes of US-Iran talks and the 10-year Treasury yield eased 4 basis points to 4.89%. S&P 500 futures are down 0.35% and Nasdaq-100 futures down 1.09% this morning.",
   "why": "About 25% of your portfolio is in US stocks, and the largest part is in S&P 500 funds. ES-US500RMF and K-USA-A(D) are priced at their 29 Oct NAV. The S&P 500 is down about 2.3% since then, so that fall is not yet in your dashboard numbers. The dashboard refreshes again at 11:30, when newer NAVs usually arrive.",
