   "headline": "KOSPI rebounds 2.24% after a morning slide, led by chip shares",
   "when": "Mon 2 Nov · Seoul close",
   "what": "KOSPI opened 1.62% lower, then closed up 2.24% at 5,859.08. Institutions net bought about 1.36 trillion won, while retail investors net sold about 1.41 trillion won. SK hynix rose 3.81% and Samsung Electronics rose 1.78%. October exports were $115.3 billion, with chip exports of $56.4 billion, nearly triple a year earlier. The won strengthened to 1,343.8 per dollar. The rebound followed Friday's 3.48% fall, which came on AI-spending doubts.",
   "why": "Korea is 17.8% of your portfolio, mostly SCBKEQTG. Its NAV is dated 29 Oct. The KOSPI was down 3.5% through 30 Oct and then rose 2.2% on Monday, so this morning's dashboard number sits above where the market has been. Korean chip shares are very sensitive to the US AI trade, and analysts quoted expect swings to continue this week.",
