   "headline": "Apple reports 12% revenue growth; the holiday forecast leaves investors cool",
   "when": "Mon 2 Nov · 17:00 ET",
   "what": "Apple said revenue for the quarter to 26 September was $114.5 billion, up 12%. Diluted earnings per share were $2.10, up 14%, including $0.05 from tariff refunds. Gross margin was 47.9%, about one point of it from the refunds. The quarterly dividend is $0.27 a share, payable 16 November to holders of record on 12 November. Bloomberg says the holiday forecast topped analyst estimates but did not impress investors after the recent rise in the shares.",
